00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:51.120
"For security reasons, do not
store keys in unsafe places."
The key isn't there... Oh!

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:52.950
"For security reasons, do not
store keys in unsafe places."
Shoot...

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:54.370
That's not good.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:59.410
"Hokkaido Shrine"
So, when I was a student I heard about
what it's like working in radio.

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:04.830
And I demonstrated it in front of Mr. Kureko
who was at my school giving a seminar.

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:11.250
Gamonne Houko's Explosive V Throw-In!

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:15.250
Haven't heard that in a while.

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:17.580
So, what is that pose?

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:22.580
It's a throw-in. Um, I listened to it
every week when I was in junior high.

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:25.040
And then, Mr. Kureko--

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:27.660
Oh, Miss Minare must be back.

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:28.700
Huh?

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.330
What part of Shiroishi-ku is it?

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:47.250
I... I don't...

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.540
...want to go home tonight.

00:15:56.330 --> 00:16:01.250
Hmm, I have a feeling things
aren't going to be the same anymore.

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:02.660
"Hey, you got dried squid!"

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:04.160
"Mr. Kunio Yanagawa"

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:07.160
Oh, you mean Mr. Toru Tachibana's sister.

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:08.200
Are you okay?

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:10.700
The both of them visited us yesterday.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:17.790
The Tachibanas lost their parents when they
were still young, so I felt bad for them.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:20.290
I haven't told them yet,
but my plan is to bill them

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:21.700
for treatment expenses only and nothing else.

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:25.250
You guys treat them nicely, too, okay?

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:29.000
Mr. Takarada, you're being
very generous right now.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:32.040
Mr. Tachibana was a hottie, wasn't he?

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:33.370
Oh...

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:37.370
What? She didn't want to go home?

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:38.290
Yeah.

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:43.040
Even if she fell for you at first sight,
that was fast of her to pull the woman card.

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:46.580
Hmm, well, it didn't seem like that, though.

00:16:46.580 --> 00:16:49.200
Of course I ended up taking her home.

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:52.580
But something about her was really strange...

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:53.540
Here.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:56.160
Thank you. I'd like to pay for it.

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:58.790
No, don't worry about it.

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:02.790
Oh, um...

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:03.750
Huh?

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:08.580
The radio station playing in the restaurant...
What station is it?

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:10.120
Huh? Oh...

00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:14.120
It's MRS. They play that jingle
from time to time.

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:16.830
Oh, is that so?

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:19.870
What a fun radio station, don't you think?

00:17:19.870 --> 00:17:22.450
Oh... Yes, it is.

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:25.000
It's just a regular station.

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:29.370
It's been a while since I listened to a station
that's not an Open University program.

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:32.500
I felt... excited listening to it.

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:35.500
And that was it?

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:36.700
And that was it.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.910
Oh, come on. Didn't you stop by a motel?

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:40.000
A motel?

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:41.290
I won't tell anyone!

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:44.290
I said I took her home!

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:45.830
Good morning.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:47.370
Morning!

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:49.790
Um, Mr. Nakahara...

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:51.290
Yes?

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:53.830
What? You want to take on more work?

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:57.080
"*Feeling out any trace of
an affair from their conversation."
Oh... But since we're not paying you...

00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:58.580
"*Feeling out any trace of
an affair from their conversation."
Hey, we could use the help. She can take orders.

00:17:58.580 --> 00:17:59.790
Hey, we could use the help. She can take orders.

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:03.450
Face it, Acting Manager.
You know we're in a bind.

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:05.410
Well, yeah. That's true.

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:07.830
Yes, please teach me anything.

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:10.950
Excuse me.

00:18:10.950 --> 00:18:11.950
Yes.

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:15.620
Would you like the hot chai after your meal?

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:18.500
What do you know? She's doing great.

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:21.500
I, Master Koda, have trained her well.

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:23.830
It's all wasted effort
if you're slacking, Miss Minare.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.330
Oh? Excuse me.

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:27.580
"Dream Space of Bread and Curry VOYAGER"
Thank you very much.

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:29.830
"Pachinko Himawari"
Miss Minare, want to grab a bite?

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:34.080
I promised Mizuho that I'd
cook tonight. Thanks, though.

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:37.250
Miss Koda, I look forward to
learning more from you tomorrow.

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:38.660
S-Sure.

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:40.160
You bet.

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:48.370
Her expressions are a bit gloomy,
but I'm glad she's working out.

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:52.910
Ah, it smells good.

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:55.580
I arranged some lotus root
on the pan like a pizza.

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:58.040
Creative meals are the best.

00:18:58.040 --> 00:19:02.330
That's great. It sounds like you
have a good helper now.

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:06.250
Honestly, I want to work with her
instead of Manager for good.

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:11.040
Miss Minare, I'm glad to hear
things at Voyager are going well.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.910
But please don't forget about radio.

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:17.870
I can't wait for you to start, Miss Minare!

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:20.370
Well, actually...

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:21.200
Miss Tachibana's not the only one who
has to quit when Manager comes back.

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:23.200
"We own your life until I'm recovered."
Miss Tachibana's not the only one who
has to quit when Manager comes back.

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:25.410
"Is that what you say to
someone who's saving you?"
Miss Tachibana's not the only one who
has to quit when Manager comes back.

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:27.410
"Is that what you say to
someone who's saving you?"
I have to quit, too.

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:32.450
As for radio, I've been listening to
Miss Chishiro Madoka's program

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:34.910
to familiarize myself...

00:19:34.910 --> 00:19:37.750
But basically...

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:42.450
Mr. Mato's totally overestimating me.
That's for sure.

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:45.790
Oh, please. You know you got this.

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:49.080
Let's be real, Mizuho.
You're there all the time.

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.790
She's very versatile with her skills.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:54.830
Y-Yes... She is.

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:56.700
In any case...

00:19:56.700 --> 00:19:59.580
I'm rooting for you, Miss Minare.

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:06.330
She sounded hesitant for a second...

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:08.750
Maybe she's being bullied.

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:11.000
I told you to get me bubbly water!

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:11.830
Ah!

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:12.790
"Dream Space of Bread and Curry VOYAGER"

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:14.790
"Dream Space of Bread and Curry VOYAGER"
Morning!

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:17.000
Hey, you're frying <i>zangi </i>already?

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:18.000
Yeah.

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:21.500
I was showing Miss Tachibana
how to work the deep fryer.

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:23.870
She wants you to be in charge
of customer service

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:26.370
while she serves as the assistant chef.

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:27.950
Well that's admirable.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:30.950
But you're not getting paid,
so don't feel too obligated--

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:33.200
No, it isn't like that.

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:37.160
I've been having the family meal, too.

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:39.160
And, also...

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:46.540
I know I'm only here because of my brother's
misconduct, so this might sound weird...

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:49.620
But it's so much fun working here...

00:20:49.620 --> 00:20:52.540
I want to take on a lot more.

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:54.410
Give her a little gratuity when she quits.

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:56.700
Oh, I know.

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:59.410
She's an honest and nice person.

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:04.290
At that time, everything, including my heart,
was peaceful as could be.

00:21:04.290 --> 00:21:06.750
"Dream Space of Bread and Curry VOYAGER"
But the next day...

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:10.160
Miss Minare, tell us what you think of this.

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:15.450
I made bite-size tapioca
pudding balls and fried them.

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:17.830
Let's see. Wow, a delicacy.

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:19.910
It could do with less salt.

00:21:19.910 --> 00:21:21.790
Yes, I'll do that next time.

00:21:21.790 --> 00:21:23.790
"Flower Pop'ems 400 yen"

00:21:24.370 --> 00:21:25.870
What's this on the menu...?

00:21:25.870 --> 00:21:28.750
Oh, that's the dish you tried yesterday.

00:21:28.750 --> 00:21:30.910
Remember? Miss Tachibana's creation?

00:21:30.910 --> 00:21:33.200
Mr. Nakahara liked it a lot.

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:35.040
I thought of the name.

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:37.200
I see...

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:39.910
The name sucks, but I think this is great.

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:41.750
They were really good.

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:44.250
I better go update the blog, then.

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:48.040
I'm sorry, forgive me if I
overstepped my boundaries.

00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:48.950
But I just updated it.

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:49.450
"Good morning! It seems like
Miss Koda is late..."

00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:49.950
"...so I, Tachibana, the temp staff will be
updating the blog. Forgive me if my words
aren't as exciting. Today's bread is American
sourdough from San Francisco..."

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:51.750
"Rosetta, as you can tell by the name,
is shaped like a rose. Since it's hollow
inside, you can pour in the curry
before you bite into it!"

00:21:51.750 --> 00:21:52.540
"Bread happiness level is four stars!
About the same  happiness you feel
when the film version of your favorite book
also turns out to be a gem."

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:53.250
"Miss Tachibana, you're very polite
with the customers. I'm rooting for you!"
"You're... The quiet one at Voyager, right?
Your writing is lovely, I like it."

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:54.950
"Miss Tachibana I'm glad Voyager hired
more people.  It seems like you're still
a bit stiff with the customers,
but you're very beautiful."

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:01.870
Gotta go. Today's Mizuho's birthday.

00:22:02.870 --> 00:22:06.580
Miss Minare's been distant recently.

00:22:11.750 --> 00:22:16.290
Shoot, I left the birthday cake
I bought this morning in the fridge.

00:22:16.290 --> 00:22:17.950
Can't forget that.

00:22:18.950 --> 00:22:22.120
Oh. They're still there.

00:22:22.120 --> 00:22:24.830
Why would you call my house?

00:22:24.830 --> 00:22:26.910
What do you mean?

00:22:26.910 --> 00:22:31.250
Why did you lie about staying
in the restaurant's staff room?

00:22:31.250 --> 00:22:34.330
I'm sorry, but it was obvious to me.

00:22:34.330 --> 00:22:38.750
You don't need to bring a big bag
like that to work at a curry restaurant.

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:41.160
You have a change of clothes in there, right?

00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:45.200
You're free to stay with a guy,
but don't use our restaurant to lie about it.

00:22:45.200 --> 00:22:47.540
There is no guy.

00:22:47.540 --> 00:22:49.830
You don't even know anything...

00:22:49.830 --> 00:22:52.750
Oh, all right.

00:22:52.750 --> 00:22:56.040
If you don't want to go home at all,

00:22:56.040 --> 00:22:57.660
why don't you stay at my place?

00:23:03.910 --> 00:23:06.160
"Chuya Nakahara Mobile"

00:23:06.160 --> 00:23:09.250
Wait, so what if I call him?

00:23:09.250 --> 00:23:13.370
I'm not Nakahara's girlfriend or anything.

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:17.950
What is he thinking? He's the one
who always says he likes me.

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:19.040
Ah.

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:22.040
Who's this person calling me
at such a sensitive time?!

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:23.830
Minare, it's been a while.

00:23:23.830 --> 00:23:24.830
Oh.

00:23:24.830 --> 00:23:26.830
The preparations are done.

00:23:26.830 --> 00:23:30.910
Your program starts tonight at 3:30 AM.

00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:32.830
We need to meet and rehearse.

00:23:32.830 --> 00:23:35.370
Come to Moiwayama Radio now.

00:23:35.370 --> 00:23:38.540
It's a 20-minute slot.
The title of the program is...

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:43.790
...Wave, Listen to Me!

00:23:43.950 --> 00:23:44.910
"Next Episode"

00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:45.700
"Next Episode"
The first episode is a fictitious report.

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:47.540
"Preview"
The first episode is a fictitious report.

00:23:47.540 --> 00:23:51.660
"Preview"
The reporter is a woman who just murdered
the man who betrayed her and ran away.

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:52.870
"Preview"
What is up with that scenario?

00:23:52.870 --> 00:23:57.370
"Preview"
The program will air at 3:32 AM,
without any introduction.

00:23:57.370 --> 00:24:01.080
"Preview"
There won't be any mention of
the program title, sponsors, or ads.

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:02.370
"Preview"
It'll end abruptly, too.

00:24:02.370 --> 00:24:04.450
"Preview"
We're going to put on a fake broadcast gaffe.

00:24:04.450 --> 00:24:05.700
"Preview"
That's crazy.

00:24:05.700 --> 00:24:10.000
"Preview"
I just want to play around a little
using your voice as my new toy.

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:14.000
Next, on <i>Wave, Listen to Me!</i>:
"You're Not Getting Out Alive."

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:16.950
"See you next time!"
"Illustrated by Hiroaki Samura"
